From a151ae128c552dc10f0b4aa360d4412120db59aa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artur <ganggg111@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 03:18:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Run PRO modes and video on a live Camera2 session

The viewfinder of the PRO modes now comes from Camera2, so manual ISO,
shutter and focus show live. Preview frames are AHardwareBuffers bound as
EGLImages to the external texture the renderer already draws, without
copies. Video (PRO video and plain video) records from the camera into a
persistent encoder input surface; libcamx muxes it with AAC sound into an
MP4. Hyperlapse and the software encoder stay on Camera1, whose
MediaRecorder cannot take the microphone on Droidian.

The camera keeps the screen on: a blanked screen makes mobile-power-saver
limit real-time threads to 50 ms per second and the ISP drops frames.

Signed-off-by: Artur <ganggg111@gmail.com>
